 "section_summary": "This section contains records from the U.S. Embassy in Tokyo and the State Department Division of Far Eastern Affairs spanning August through November 1934. It features comprehensive monthly reports on internal political, economic, and foreign affairs in Japan, highlighting rising friction surrounding the upcoming 1935 Naval Disarmament Conference and the Washington Naval Treaty. Major international issues documented include Chinese Eastern Railway sale negotiations with the Soviet Union, Japanese administrative reorganization in Manchuria, American oil industry tensions under the Petroleum Industry Law, and anti-Japanese demonstrations in Arizona.",
